From af3b84361d9dfbcc39dd42a95db109186cb915a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:32:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] L1 threads: exiting threads leave the scheduler and are
 reaped before the next holder runs; futures hash and lock by creation order

An exiting thread's teardown consumed seeded choices and ran concurrently with
the next holder. concurrent.futures iterates sets of futures and locks them in
id() order, so which future was seen first followed the heap layout (easypy
test_multiobject_1: 3 fingerprints in 25 runs, now 1 in 16).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAF6Dgp7MTxUYBRZseFL3V
---
 python/detpy/threads.py | 85 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/test_threads.py   | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

